## Part 1: the contact sheets (Check task)

The role read each of the 51 rows of the 7 `family/pictures.sha256` files. It derived the kind
from the source name: `card-kit-patch-` is patch, `card-kit-dots-` is dots, and `l2-w0N-card-`
is card when the card folder holds it and forge when the Forge folder holds it. `family` (w04)
is in both folders and takes `card` (H3). Kind counts: card 16, patch 7, dots 10, forge 18.

The script is `/tmp/opencode/p10_contact.py`. The build ran in one heavy-run wrapper. The
capture `p10-contact-build.txt` ends with the 4 sheet sizes and `tiles.tsv lines: 51`.

| Sheet | Tiles | Pixels |
|---|---|---|
| `p10-contact/p10-contact-1-card.png` | 16 | 2024 x 1312 |
| `p10-contact/p10-contact-2-patch-dots.png` | 17 | 1560 x 1512 |
| `p10-contact/p10-contact-3-forge-a.png` | 8 | 2128 x 1308 |
| `p10-contact/p10-contact-4-forge-b.png` | 10 | 2008 x 1632 |

- Each tile holds the output JPEG and, for card and forge, the source PNG. A patch or dots tile
  holds the JPEG only, because code draws its source.
- The label holds week, word, kind, source name, and JPEG name. The values come from the week
  files and `pictures.sha256`, not from the hand.
- `tiles.tsv` holds 51 lines with no header: week, word, kind, source name, JPEG name, JPEG
  SHA-256, and pixel size, separated by one tab.
- Each JPEG is 800 x 800, and each JPEG SHA-256 equals its provenance line. The script stops on
  a difference.
- Writes: the run folder and `/tmp/opencode/` only. The hand-off folders are read-only.

The orchestrator person check (AC10-10) passed 51 of 51 on 2026-11-07. The result is on the
Check task line.

## Part 2: the Package build

Source commit: `a5fa259f` (the commit that holds all 51 `"file"` lines). The build read each
payload file with `git show a5fa259f:content/storytime/<path>` (rule R4). The script is
`/tmp/opencode/p10_package_build.py`; the check script is `/tmp/opencode/p10_package_check.py`.

