## Deviations

1. Rule R4: the 4 w01 song files (`l2/media/w01/song.mp4`, `song-phone.mp4`,
   `song-poster.jpg`, `song-phone-poster.jpg`) are not in git at `a5fa259f`. The build read them
   from `w01-storytime-app-package-r2` (read-only), never from the work tree. Their SHA-256
   values equal that folder and the work tree: `4c88951f`, `74ccefed`, `abef5e06`, `47365f31`.
   Check 9 names `song-phone-poster.jpg` as the local file that must be present.
2. No implementation commit: the build output lives outside the repo. The run evidence is in
   commit dd234147. The plan evidence commit holds `plan.md` and this log, because a commit
   cannot hold its own SHA.
3. The first build attempt failed on the first git-absent file. The role removed the partial
   `w01-storytime-app-package-r3` folder that the attempt created, then reran. The create-only
   rule held at the start and at the rerun.
4. Pre-check 4 of the Forge delivery accepted `duck` and `horse`. The person check names them
   as white subjects. No gate ran tsc in this task, so the tsc exception does not apply.
5. The plan edit went in through the shell (python), because the measure-guard refuses a direct
   edit.

